      "side": 1,
      "message": "init_flags are flags set at init\n\nIt this possible to not add the setter but re-init the flags instead ? like we are doing in some [tests](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/modules/Bluetooth/system/device/test/device_iot_config_test.cc;l\u003d37;drc\u003df36760dd382fef4352f4aaaadef6367163d8c8af)\n\nThe reason for that is that some flags are only checked at init of some modules / stack. So changing them after started the stack will be a no-op.\nBy adding the setter we are saying to the dev \"go-on any flag can be updated this way\" which is false.\n\nI am throwing a curve ball here but:\nShould we instead cut the flags in 2 categories, one dynamic runtime flags that can change anytime, and the other only at init time.",
      "revId": "f2895081e5f4a89cb8e0eda2c6795c22f0391ee1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
